1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Enterprise context is scattered across screens, APIs, and repositories. Context IQ turns trusted product capabilities into safe conversational workflows.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Installation starts with one command. Point Context IQ at an existing React and .NET repository, choose the product and assistant names, and keep generated work isolated.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Now the assistant is running live. A user asks for recent requests and receives grounded results from registered, typed tools.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The selected request opens in the product view. Conversational context carries the same trusted identifier into the next step.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Context IQ resolves the related review ticket and opens the review queue with validated navigation. It never invents missing identifiers or silently performs mutations.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The generated repository dashboard shows discovered APIs, read-only classifications, UI routes, and suggested queries for product-owner review.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The architecture keeps trust boundaries clear. React owns visible context, Context IQ owns typed orchestration, and authorized .NET APIs enforce product policy.

8
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:15,800
The result is a reusable path from repository discovery to a governed assistant, generated integration scaffolding, and regression scenarios.
